# murder — fail
#
# The murder verb attempted and missed: checks pass, the dice do not.
#
# Reached in 1/12 of the sampled location ids, with REAL schedules (no --npc-static).
# That flag pins everyone to their workplace all day, which is exactly what this verb cannot have:
# it needs somebody asleep in their own bed, and a pinned NPC never goes to bed.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Room" --period night --observe-only "weaver"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy fail-dice
goal murder
advance 12 180
regions

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect FAILURE

# What makes this a murder test rather than an any-verb test.
expect-verb murder
# The failure assertion that means something: the verb's own consequence did NOT happen.
# Asserting the wound instead would be flaky — FailurePenalties samples one slot in five,
# so most failures injure nobody.
expect-no-outcome npc_slayn
quit
